#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Visual shape clustering + magnitude sequences from Ghostty packed rasters.

Re-reads the *current* packed PNGs (the post-stack-change set). Does not use
Unicode names for clustering. Names appear only as captions after the fact.

Scope: measured glyphs with cp < U+3000, minus Hangul Jamo (U+1100–11FF) and
the CJK-radical tail (U+2E80–2FFF). That is the symbol / math / latin / shape /
punctuation panel, not CJK-weighted occupancy k-means.

Clustering is from pixels:
  - convex-hull circularity, aspect, holes, component count, relative size
  - 8×8 bbox-normalized occupancy
  then a coarse *visual family* (circle / dot / square / bar / multi-dot / other)
  and k-means subclusters inside each family.

Magnitude of a series is one or a combination of:
  - density gradient (optical coverage)
  - size gradient (bounding-box area)
  - both (density and size track the same order)
  - intrinsic gradient (number systems / enclosed numerics / digit value)

A family page shows the same glyphs under density, size, and code-point sorts.
A sequence is tagged with whichever of those channels actually hold.

Does not write into axes/. Does not retouch bmp-metrics*.tsv or .rasters/.

Usage:
    ./cluster-visual
    ./cluster-visual --out gallery
"""

